>Ciprofloxacin and trimethoprim cause phage induction and virulence modulation in <italic>Staphylococcus aureus</italic>.</article-title><source>Antimicrob Agents Chemother</source><volume>50</volume><fpage>171</fpage><lpage>177</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16377683</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests: </bold>Three of the paper's authors (F.T., M.-F.P., and H.M.K.) are authors of a patent application (PCT/IB2007/000880), filed under the Patent Cooperation Treaty (PCT), involving some of the work presented in this paper.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding: </bold>This work was supported by the CNRS and by a grant from the Minist&#x000e8;re de la Recherche (ACI-Microbiology Biodefense Initiative).</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>